# Service360 EC2 deploy (mandatory)

**Server:** `13.55.122.55` (`/opt/app`, branch `main`). Containers: `deploy-api-1` (:5301), `deploy-admin-1` (:80).

## NEVER on EC2

- `docker compose build` / full docker rebuild (OOM, 30+ min)
- `git reset --hard` or full repo sync as part of deploy
- React/npm compile on the server
- Cron jobs that build containers (`ec2-auto-deploy.sh` is disabled — exit 0)

## ALWAYS deploy changed code only

1. **Build off-server:** GitHub Actions `deploy-fast.yml` OR local `deploy/PUSH-CHANGED.cmd` / `deploy/scripts/deploy-changed.ps1`
2. **Ship compiled output only:** `dist/` (API) or `build/` (admin) tarball → SCP → `ec2-apply-artifacts.sh api|admin`
3. **Server step (~30 sec):** `docker cp` into running container + `docker restart` — nothing else

## What triggers what

| Changed path | Build | Skip |
|--------------|-------|------|
| `service_link_api-main/**` | API only | admin |
| `service_link_admin-main/**` | Admin only | api |
| docs / unrelated | nothing | both |

## If user asks to deploy

Run or instruct: `deploy\PUSH-CHANGED.cmd` (auto-detect) or `-Target api|admin`.

Do not suggest `ec2-deploy.sh`, `docker compose up --build`, or SSH git pull as deploy.

## Stability (already on server)

Swap 2GB, docker memory limits in `deploy/docker-compose.aws-test.yml`, `ec2-watchdog.sh` cron.
